{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I ain't got no [G]home, I'm [C]just a-roamin' [G]'round,
[G]Just a wandrin' [G]worker, I [D]go from town to [D]town.
And the [G]police make it [G]hard [C]wherever I may [G]go
And I [G]ain't got no [G]home in this [D]world [G]anymore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My brothers and my sisters are stranded on this road,
A hot and dusty road that a million feet have trod;
Rich man took my home and drove me from my door
And I ain't got no home in this world anymore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Was a-farmin' on the shares, and always I was poor;
My crops I lay into the banker's store.
My wife took down and died upon the cabin floor,
And I ain't got no home in this world anymore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Now as I look around, it's mighty plain to see
This world is such a great and a funny place to be;
Oh, the gamblin' man is rich an' the workin' man is poor,
And I ain't got no home in this world anymore.
{end_of_verse}
